there're three objects, iterable object, iterator object, and generator object
they all can have for loop to iterate
but iterable object like list, it can iterate multiple times
a = [1,2,3]
for i in a
    print(i)

for i in a
    print(i)

iterable object a can do a lot times,

but iterator object like filter, and generator object, they only iterate once,

b = filter(lambda x: x, [1,2,3])
for i in b:
    print(i)
after this for loop, b become empty list []
so does generator,

generator object is created by yield, iterator and generator object only iterate once by for




